yes, when creating a new gear...<br><br>1. The things connected to the cylinder need to be fix up first<br><br>2. Create the cylinder, add the constraints.(object buttons F7, add constraint, select hinge constraint, hit "show pivot",  the hinge pivots on the px axis)<br><br>3. In the cylinders logic buttons Select "compound"<br><br>4. Add a cube<br><br>5. Set the bounds of cube to cube<br><br>6. On the cube use alt-r then ctrl-a then alt-p(clear the "clear parent inverse" do this BEFORE parenting it to the cylinder.<br><br>7. Parent the cube to the cylinder<br><br>hope that works.. and helps<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1343">Appolonius</a> — Mon Jan 15, 2007 11:17 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
